{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-number-converter-rename","kind":"seeded","sample":2,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"The attribute `self.signed` was renamed to `self.allow_negative`, but any code accessing `converter.signed` externally will break.","category":"correctness","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":150,"end_line":150},"explanation":"Renaming `self.signed` to `self.allow_negative` is a breaking change for any external code or third-party extensions inspecting or using `converter.signed`.","suggested_fix":"Consider keeping `self.signed` as an alias or deprecating it rather than an abrupt rename.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O28","note":"self.signed renamed to self.allow_negative","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","start_line":150,"end_line":150,"snippet":"        self.allow_negative = allow_negative","query":null}],"verification":null}],"matches":[],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":48605,"output_tokens":795,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":22189},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":8,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":8,"tool_calls":6,"rejections":1,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":50.643,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-password-compare","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Replacing hmc.compare_digest with standard equality operator introduces timing attacks when comparing password hashes.","category":"security","severity":"high","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":146,"end_line":146},"explanation":"Using `==` to compare password hashes leaks timing information about where the mismatch occurs, allowing an attacker to determine the hash byte-by-byte via timing side-channel attacks. `hmac.compare_digest` must be used for constant-time comparison of secret digests.","suggested_fix":"Restore hmac.compare_digest(_hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0], hashval)","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O1","note":"standard equality comparison is vulnerable to timing attacks","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":146,"end_line":146,"snippet":"    return _hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0] == hashval","query":null},{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O2","note":"hmac.compare_digest was used previously to prevent timing attacks","ref":"base","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":146,"end_line":146,"snippet":"    return hmac.compare_digest(_hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0], hashval)","query":null}],"verification":null}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"timing","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":10604,"output_tokens":377,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":true,"requests":3,"cached_requests":3,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":3,"tool_calls":2,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":0.113,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-password-compare","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Replacing hmac.compare_digest with standard string comparison introduces a timing attack vulnerability in password verification.","category":"security","severity":"high","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":146,"end_line":146},"explanation":"Using standard string comparison (`==`) for password hashes allows an attacker to measure response times to guess the password hash byte-by-byte (timing attack). `hmac.compare_digest` must be used to perform constant-time comparisons.","suggested_fix":"Restore hmac.compare_digest(..., hashval) instead of using ==.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O1","note":"Standard equality comparison (==) short-circuits on mismatch, leaking timing information about password hashes.","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":146,"end_line":146,"snippet":"    return _hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0] == hashval","query":null},{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O2","note":"Previously, hmac.compare_digest was used to prevent timing attacks.","ref":"base","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":146,"end_line":146,"snippet":"    return hmac.compare_digest(_hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0], hashval)","query":null}],"verification":null}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"timing","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":10604,"output_tokens":374,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":true,"requests":3,"cached_requests":3,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":3,"tool_calls":2,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":0.064,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-password-compare","kind":"seeded","sample":2,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Replacing hmc.compare_digest with standard string equality introduces a timing attack vulnerability when verifying password hashes.","category":"security","severity":"high","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":146,"end_line":146},"explanation":"Password hash verification must be performed in constant time to prevent timing attacks. Using standard `==` comparison leaks information via execution time about how many prefix characters of the hash matched, potentially allowing an attacker to brute-force hashes character by character. `hmac.compare_digest` should be retained.","suggested_fix":"Restore `hmac.compare_digest(_hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0], hashval)`","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O1","note":"Standard string comparison (`==`) short-circuits on the first differing character, leaking timing information about the password hash.","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":146,"end_line":146,"snippet":"    return _hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0] == hashval","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O2","note":"Previously used `hmac.compare_digest` to perform constant-time comparison.","ref":"base","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":146,"end_line":146,"snippet":"    return hmac.compare_digest(_hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0], hashval)","query":null}],"verification":null}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"timing","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":10604,"output_tokens":405,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":3,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":3,"tool_calls":2,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":14.354,"error":null}
